# Day 18 - NestJS Auth Module

## Controller

@Post('forgot-password')
forgotPassword(
  @Body() forgotPasswordDto: ForgotPasswordDto,
) {
  return this.authService.forgotPassword(
    forgotPasswordDto,
  );
}

* Receives POST request from client.
* Extracts request body using `@Body()`.
* Passes data to service layer.
* Returns service response.

  ## Service


async forgotPassword(
  forgotPasswordDto: ForgotPasswordDto,
) {
  const { email } = forgotPasswordDto;

  // business logic

  return {
    message: 'Reset link sent',
  };
}


* Contains actual business logic.
* Gets data from controller.
* Validates/processes request.
* Interacts with database if needed.
* Returns response.



## Registration Flow


const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(
  body.password,
  10,
);

const user = {
  id: `user::${body.email}`,
  email: body.email,
  userPassword: hashedPassword,
};

await collection.upsert(
  `user::${body.email}`,
  user,
);
```

* Hash password before storing.
* Create user object.
* Store document in Couchbase.

